  "reasoning": "The defendants accepted large sums of money in exchange for illegally registering non‑eligible candidates for the provincial college entrance examination, which constitutes bribery (受贿). Their actions of violating enrollment regulations to favor certain students constitute the crime of abusing official duties for personal gain, i.e., the \"徇私舞弊罪\" (abuse of power in student enrollment). Additionally, the defendant who fabricated official school and public security bureau seals and produced false academic and household registration certificates committed the crime of forging state documents, i.e., 伪造国家机关公文罪. Therefore, the appropriate charges are bribery, abuse of power in student enrollment, and forgery of state documents.",
  "final_answer": "[罪名]受贿;徇私舞弊罪;伪造国家机关公文罪<eoa>"
}

